    "accountability",
    "tolerating bad behavior",
    "team culture",
    "Christian leadership"
  ],
  "og_image": "/assets/og/what-the-leader-tolerates.png",
  "scriptures": [
    {
      "ref": "1 Corinthians 5:6",
      "text": "Don’t you know that a little yeast leavens the whole batch of dough?"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1 Samuel 3:13",
      "text": "For I told him that I would judge his family forever because of the sin he knew about; his sons blasphemed God, and he failed to restrain them."
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "the_revelation",
      "label": "The Revelation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Not every culture problem begins because a leader endorsed something."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sometimes the leader simply:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "DID NOTHING."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Everyone knew."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The disrespect.",
            "The gossip.",
            "The bullying.",
            "The dishonesty.",
            "The manipulation.",
            "The inappropriate behavior.",
            "The toxic high performer."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But confronting it would be difficult."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "So leadership waited.",
            "And waited."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Eventually silence communicated something:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "THIS CAN HAPPEN HERE."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_lie",
      "label": "The Lie",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“IF I DON’T ADDRESS IT, MAYBE IT WILL GO AWAY.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sometimes patience is wisdom."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Not every issue requires immediate intervention."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But chronic avoidance isn’t patience."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Especially when the pattern is harming people."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because every time obvious dysfunction occurs without meaningful response, the room receives information."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The offender learns:",
            "I can continue."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The harmed person learns:",
            "Nobody will protect this boundary."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The observer learns:",
            "Don’t expect leadership to act."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "SILENCE BECOMES A SIGNAL."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "eli",
      "label": "Eli",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Eli’s sons were corrupt."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And Scripture’s indictment includes:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“he failed to restrain them.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Eli didn’t need to participate in their behavior to become responsible for his failure to address what was happening under his authority."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s sobering leadership territory."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sometimes:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "THE SIN OF LEADERSHIP ISN’T WHAT THE LEADER DID. IT’S WHAT THE LEADER REFUSED TO CONFRONT."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_truth",
      "label": "The Truth",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "WHAT YOU TOLERATE REPEATEDLY CAN BECOME WHAT YOU NORMALIZE CULTURALLY."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "One disrespectful comment.",
            "Maybe correction."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Repeated disrespect without correction?",
            "Now the room learns."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "One dishonest report.",
            "Investigate."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Repeated dishonesty ignored because the person produces?",
            "Now everyone learns:",
            "performance matters more than integrity."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This is how drift happens."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Not usually through a meeting where everyone votes:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“Let’s abandon our values.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But through:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "exception.",
            "avoidance.",
            "delay.",
            "another exception.",
            "another accommodation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "until:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHAT ONCE WOULD HAVE SHOCKED THE CULTURE NOW SIMPLY DESCRIBES IT."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "but_dont_become_a_culture_police_officer",
      "label": "But Don’t Become a Culture Police Officer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Another guardrail."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Leadership isn’t constant suspicion."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Not every mistake needs public correction.",
            "Not every irritation is sin.",
            "Not every disagreement is rebellion."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Wise leaders distinguish:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "preference.",
            "immaturity.",
            "mistake.",
            "pattern.",
            "sin.",
            "danger."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The goal isn’t control."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "THE GOAL IS FAITHFUL STEWARDSHIP."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_audit",
      "label": "The Audit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "items": [
            "WHAT DO I KNOW IS HAPPENING THAT I KEEP AVOIDING?",
            "WHY?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Fear of conflict?",
            "Fear of losing someone?",
            "Money?",
            "Numbers?",
            "Friendship?",
            "Reputation?",
            "Convenience?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHO IS PAYING THE PRICE FOR MY AVOIDANCE?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s often the forgotten question."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Because the leader experiences the comfort of avoiding confrontation,",
            "while somebody else experiences the cost."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_surrender",
      "label": "The Surrender",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Identify one thing you’ve been calling:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“patience”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "that may actually be:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "AVOIDANCE."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Pray.",
            "Get counsel.",
            "Gather facts.",
            "Then respond appropriately."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Not emotionally.",
            "Not vindictively.",
            "Faithfully."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because love sometimes requires a conversation you’ve been hoping you wouldn’t have to have."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "take_it_with_you",
      "label": "Take It With You",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "What leadership repeatedly refuses to confront eventually receives permission to remain."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_prayer",
      "label": "The Prayer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Father,"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Give me wisdom to distinguish patience from avoidance."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Courage to confront what harms the people entrusted to me."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Keep me from protecting comfort at someone else’s expense."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Give me truth without aggression.",
            "Courage without ego.",
            "Accountability without humiliation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And wisdom to know when to wait and when faithfulness requires action."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "In Jesus name,",
            "Amen."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "hidden_gems",
      "label": "Hidden Gems 💎",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "Silence becomes a signal."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "What leadership repeatedly refuses to confront eventually receives permission to remain."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Sometimes the sin of leadership isn’t what the leader did. It’s what the leader refused to confront."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Who is paying the price for my avoidance?"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "What once would have shocked the culture can eventually simply describe it."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Love sometimes requires a conversation you’ve been hoping you wouldn’t have to have."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "-TheWrkShop"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "__insert_block_header": "2026-10-20_1-corinthians-5-6_what-the-leader-tolerates|"
}
